                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "814ae8c4-589a-37c6-8d26-8bce3eee2007",
                        "entry_id": "d94b93d3-2f5b-3279-8785-67131d192dac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To assemble a project in a hasty, sloppy manner, especially using cheap, inferior or improvised materials."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bd06dc0-05e7-4603-b179-011cdd441125",
                                "sense_id": "814ae8c4-589a-37c6-8d26-8bce3eee2007",
                                "text": "It was a queer-looking hovel, built of galvanised iron and kerosene-cans and bark and saplings and bamboo, according to no definite plan, and obviously, to knowing eyes, by one of those masters of the craft of jerry-building […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5261a749-236b-41b0-8fcb-50db59c5077c",
                                "sense_id": "814ae8c4-589a-37c6-8d26-8bce3eee2007",
                                "text": "If we look at some of the stories of R. D. Laing's patients in The Politics of Experience it looks as if schizophrenia jerrybuilds a shaky structure of passion and freedom which depends for existence on negation of control and conscious scruple."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6239e442-d5aa-4494-8467-28fa8ef3ddb1",
                                "sense_id": "814ae8c4-589a-37c6-8d26-8bce3eee2007",
                                "text": "Evolution, for example, isn't rational—and it jerry-builds our bodies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3334dc73-1337-4901-854b-a1f981a3cd46",
                                "sense_id": "814ae8c4-589a-37c6-8d26-8bce3eee2007",
                                "text": "Little wonder that corners were cut, bad materials made do for good and jerry-building was one of the curses of the age."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc4e36ee-d820-336f-bd2a-9cf1d0ad172f",
                        "entry_id": "d94b93d3-2f5b-3279-8785-67131d192dac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To assemble a structure in such an unsafe manner that it is doomed to collapse."
                        ],
